      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64298,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>Most lesions are asymptomatic, but they may present as polyps or be associated with chronic cervicitis and mucous discharge. Large or deeply situated nabothian cysts can be clinically concerning for a malignant process.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T18:16:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64299,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nabothian cysts are common, especially in multiparous women.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64300,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64301,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Obstruction of an endocervical gland leads to mucus retention and cyst formation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64302,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nabothian cysts are single or multiple, filled with mucus, and usually 2&ndash;10&nbsp;mm in diameter. They are generally near the mucosal surface but are occasionally located deep in the cervical wall {2807713}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64303,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cystic spaces are round to slightly irregular and lined by a single layer of non-atypical attenuated to columnar endocervical-type epithelium. There is sometimes tubal metaplasia. No associated stromal reaction is noted. Deep nabothian cysts may be rarely identified {2807713}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64304,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
